# The trial of pod-netstack in podnet (T-023, the cut of PodUtils/podnet#427).
# podnet-vnet takes the stack and the link devices of pod-netstack in place
# of stack.rs, stack/reactor.rs, stack/service.rs, stack/socket.rs,
# stack/datagrams.rs and device.rs: stack and device give them at their old
# paths, VnetDatagrams is UdpDatagrams, TunnelDevice stays an alias, and
# RecordingDevice<D> is the device of pod-netstack with the Recorder as its
# PacketTap. Acl implements Admit (the admit of StackConfig), Resolver
# implements GatewayService (port 53 at the gateway), VirtualSubnet converts
# to and from Subnet. stack/proof.rs (net doctor) stays; the tests of the cut
# leave stack/tests.rs and device.rs. Each smoltcp of podnet moves from
# =0.12.0 to 0.14 (one version in the tree); tests/tcp_window.rs gives its
# sockets no congestion controller, as the stacks of podnet. Each podcrates
# tag moves to v0.20.0. The record, the size and the layers of the files,
# the build, the bans and the sources of cargo-deny, one smoltcp, no copy of
# the moved items left in podnet, clippy of the workspace, the docs of
# podnet-vnet, the tests of each crate (podnet-vnet: the stack, the switch,
# the dialer, the door, the proof, the hooks), the library of podnet (WARP
# on smoltcp 0.14), the integration tests of the vnet, of the window and of
# the pod (seccomp and netns: the large download of T-226), doctor, docs and
# the API, the fuzz targets with their lock, rustfmt, each Rust toolchain of
# the workflows and build images against the rust-version of podcrates, and
# the binary for x86_64 musl, built with zig (a debug build: the release
# profile takes LTO), with podnet's static check of it.
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- remap Cargo.lock > /dev/null
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- check
python3 scripts/check-size.py
python3 scripts/check-layers.py
grep -q '^SMOLTCP_IFACE_MAX_ADDR_COUNT = "8"$' .cargo/config.toml
cargo build -q
command -v cargo-deny > /dev/null || cargo install -q --locked cargo-deny
cargo deny --locked check bans sources
cargo tree -q -p podnet-vnet -i pod-netstack > /dev/null
test "$(grep -c '^name = "smoltcp"$' Cargo.lock)" = 1
! test -e crates/podnet-vnet/src/stack/reactor.rs
! git grep -n -E "struct Core\b|fn service_conns|struct LinkTx|fn new_tcp_socket|struct QueueInner|fn spawn_listener_socket" -- crates src
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
RUSTDOCFLAGS="-D warnings" cargo doc -q --no-deps -p podnet-vnet
cargo test -q -p podnet-vnet
cargo test -q -p podnet-netns -p podnet-core -p podnet-serve
cargo test -q -p podnet --lib
cargo test -q -p podnet --test vnet --test vnet_regressions --test vnet_proxy_forward --test tcp_window --test shim_direct --test shim_socks --test shim_no_socket --test shim_datagram_user
cargo test -q -p podnet --test pod_seccomp --test pod_seccomp_tcp --test pod_seccomp_dgram --test pod_seccomp_fds --test pod_seccomp_handoff --test pod_seccomp_nonblock --test pod_seccomp_rules --test pod_seccomp_slow_dial --test pod_seccomp_diff --test pod_backend_line --test pod_usage --test af_inet_kernel --test doctor --test docs --test api_surface
cargo update -q -w --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml
cargo check -q --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml --bins
cargo fmt --all --check
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
cargo zigbuild -q --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl -p podnet --bin podnet
sh scripts/check-static.sh "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podnet"
